  "lineage": "Tarantella napoletana Southern Italian folk-dance-and-song tradition of the Naples region (Campania), characterized by fast 6/8 meter (or compound-duple), virtuoso mandolin-and-acoustic-guitar instrumental lead, and tambourine percussion (the tammorra and tamburello). Historically connected to the tarantismo ritual-healing dance-cure tradition of southern Italian rural communities (the dance ostensibly cured tarantism, the psychosomatic illness attributed to tarantula-bite). Performance contexts span village-festival celebrations, weddings, and the canonical Neapolitan urban-popular concertina contexts. Distinguished from pizzica salentina by tarantella napoletana's Campanian regional cadential-conventions and the broader Neapolitan canzone connection.",
